Subject: [RFC] Switch default merge backend from recursive to ort

I think we should switch the default merge backend from recursive to
ort.  From experience, switching is smooth, easy, and basically
problem free.  "Past performance isn't a guarantee of future results",
to borrow a phrase from the financial world, but I think it's ready.

Reasons the switch is safe:
  * There's an easy fallback
  * Passes all tests that recursive does, and dozens it doesn't
  * <Real-world testing at Palantir, including --remerge-diff default>
  * <Specialized testing I do>

Advantages of ort:
  * Faster (dramatically so)
  * More correct (as noted above)
  * Better design
  * New features
    * AUTO_MERGE
    * --remerge-diff
    * an important component towards enabling sparse indexes
    * reducing need to download blobs for partial clones (due to only
      detecting renames for relevant_sources)
    * cherry-pick/rebase in a bare repository


